From 3ab0142219b33b0b02523de51b385ebdbfbb3940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:05:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add error monitoring and rate limiting on the AI-calling
 endpoints
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- server/monitoring.ts: thin wrapper around @sentry/node. No-ops entirely
  until SENTRY_DSN is set in Vercel, so this ships with zero behavior
  change for anyone who hasn't configured it yet. Wired into
  server/http.ts's fail() so unexpected server errors (5xx, and the
  generic 400s this app uses for most thrown errors) get reported instead
  of only sitting in Vercel's function logs. 401/403 are excluded since
  those are normal auth/permission outcomes, not incidents.
- supabase/migrations/016_rate_limits.sql + server/ratelimit.ts: adds a
  per-user rate limit backed by a Postgres function (atomic upsert, so
  concurrent requests from the same user can't race past the limit the
  way a select-then-update from application code could). Applied to
  api/audio/transcribe.ts (20 recordings / 10 min / user) and
  api/commands/interpret.ts (30 commands / 10 min / user) — the two
  endpoints that call OpenAI and were previously uncapped. Fails open
  (allows the request) if the check itself errors, since this is a
  cost/abuse guard, not a security boundary.
- No new external account required for any of this to deploy safely;
  Sentry only activates once SENTRY_DSN is added, and rate limiting uses
  Supabase you already have rather than a new Redis provider.

Verified: npm run typecheck, npx vitest run (19 passing), and
npm run build:web all pass.

